1043:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the I2C data
1044:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****     transfers.
1045:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
1046:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
1047:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) Blocking mode : The communication is performed in the polling mode.
1048:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The status of all data processing is returned by the same function
1049:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****             after finishing transfer.
1050:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) No-Blocking mode : The communication is performed using Interrupts
1051:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****             or DMA. These functions return the status of the transfer startup.
1052:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
1053:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****             dedicated I2C IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
1054:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****             using DMA mode.
1055:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
1056:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_i2c.c ****     (#) Blocking mode functions are :
